# =====================================================================================================
# TalentLoop FRONTEND environment (React + Vite)
# =====================================================================================================
#
# The frontend needs NO environment variables and holds NO secrets. Everything it needs (the Vapi public
# key, model names, feature flags) comes from the backend at run time through /api/health and the
# interview endpoints. That way a key never ends up baked into public JavaScript.
#
# The only frontend setting is WHERE THE BACKEND IS:
#
#  - One Render service (recommended): nothing to set. The backend serves the website itself.
#
#  - Frontend on Vercel: edit frontend/vercel.json and replace YOUR-BACKEND.onrender.com (2 places)
#    with your Render service address. Vercel then forwards /api and /media to Render, so the browser
#    talks to a single address and sign-in cookies work. Also set APP_URL on the BACKEND to your
#    Vercel address (see deploy/backend.env.example).
#
#  - Local development (npm run dev): Vite forwards /api, /media and /llm to http://127.0.0.1:8000
#    (vite.config.ts). Start the backend on port 8000 first.
#
# Vercel > Project > Settings > Environment Variables: leave empty.
